fact WorkItem(id: "WI-187", description: some(value: "FileStore source-span retract: introduce IndexedStore<Location> trait + IndexedFileStore implementation, replace canonical-keyed retract with span-based. Today's content-keyed retract path (file_store.rs apply_retracts: parse each file, print each fact head, string-compare to retract canonicals) breaks for any entity with optional named-args, because TermPrinter::print_term against the live KB produces a loader-normalized string (logical vars filling unspecified fields, list-literal desugaring, constructor named-arg expansion) while TermPrinter::over(parsed) produces a parse-form string — the two never string-equal. Concrete failure: WI-009 phase-3 cmd_claim retracts the old WorkItem(... status: Open) but the source workitems.anthill block stays untouched on disk; new Claimed fact lands in facts.anthill; on next pull both load → duplicate WI-001. Fix: a per-store source map populated at pull time. Work: (a) define `pub trait IndexedStore: Store { type Location: Clone; fn location_of(&self, id: RuleId) -> Option<Self::Location>; }` in persistence/mod.rs; (b) `IndexedFileStore` struct composing FileStore + `source_map: HashMap<RuleId, (PathBuf, Span)>`, with `pull_with_source(&mut KnowledgeBase)` that loads each .anthill file and records every fact's (rule_id, fact_span) pair; (c) loader: extend `LoadResult` with `fact_rule_ids: Vec<RuleId>` in source order so the store can pair fact spans with the RuleIds the loader allocated; (d) `ParsedFile::fact_spans()` helper; (e) `IndexedFileStore::Store::retract` consults `source_map` first, falls back to FileStore's content-keyed path for runtime-asserted facts (no source); (f) bundle's `run_anthill_bundle` switches the registered store from FileStore to IndexedFileStore. Driver: WI-009 phase 3 (cmd_claim, cmd_deliver, cmd_verify, cmd_update, cmd_delete, cmd_add_dependency, cmd_remove_dependency) needs in-place retract of source-loaded facts. The fresh_var, find_fact, replace_named_arg builtins (WI-182, WI-009 phase-3 prereq) are already landed and will be reused. Other indexable-store backends (IndexedSqlStore with Location=RowId, IndexedDuckDbStore with Location=(Table, PrimaryKey), IndexedGitStore with Location=(BlobHash, Path)) fall out of the same trait shape — out of scope here but the trait is designed to admit them. Future alternative: append-only event-log store (assert/retract events in a journal, hash-cons identity for retract matching after replay) — captured as a follow-up, not blocking. Acceptance: ports cmd_claim end-to-end such that running `anthill-todo --anthill claim WI-001` against a project with `fact WorkItem(id: \"WI-001\", ..., status: Open)` produces a single WorkItem(id: \"WI-001\", ..., status: Claimed(...)) on disk (Open block dropped, Claimed block written); cargo-test green; existing persistence_test cases untouched."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-20T19:45:11Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-187", author: "claude", content: "Already implemented in prior commits (38e709d WI-187 + WI-009 phase 3: IndexedFileStore + cmd_claim; ecae0b1 simplify pass; extended by 4c08e87 WI-202). IndexedStore trait (persistence/mod.rs:127) + IndexedFileStore (indexed_file_store.rs) with source_map, span-based retract, byte-range-dropping flush, by_id index. Bundle registers it in run_anthill_bundle (main.rs:1746), seeding source_map by zipping LoadResult.fact_rule_ids (load.rs:1408) with fact spans. Acceptance met: cmd_claim_test::claim_drops_open_block_and_writes_claimed spawns real 'anthill-todo --anthill claim WI-001' in a tempdir, asserts Open block dropped + single Claimed fact written. Verified green 2026-05-20: anthill-todo suite 33 pass; anthill-core builtin_tests 53 + wi_tests 123 (incl persistence_test/persistence_builtins_test/wi202_retrieve_test). No new code needed; marking delivered.", at: "2026-05-20T19:45:04Z")
